#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Keeps the docs self-updating: a commit that changes app, editor or script
# code must also touch README.md, CLAUDE.md or docs/ in the same commit.
# Add [skip docs] to the message only when nothing user-visible, architectural
# or workflow-related changed (pure refactor, typo, internal bug fix).
# Enabled by scripts/setup.sh (git config core.hooksPath scripts/githooks).
set -euo pipefail
msg_file="$1"
grep -qiF '[skip docs]' "$msg_file" && exit 0
files=$(git diff --cached --name-only)
echo "$files" | grep -qE '^(Notez/|editor/src/|scripts/)' || exit 0
echo "$files" | grep -qE '^(README\.md|CLAUDE\.md|docs/)' && exit 0
cat >&2 <<'MSG'
Commit blocked: code changed but no docs did.
Update in this same commit, as relevant:
  README.md            Features list (one line per feature) and shortcuts
  docs/FEATURES.md     how it works, ✅/🟡 status, known limitations
  docs/ARCHITECTURE.md models, store, bridge, flows, build/release
  CLAUDE.md            new rules, scripts, gotchas, lessons learned
If nothing user-visible or architectural changed, add [skip docs] to the message.
MSG
exit 1
